        openings: ("After a no-contact order was entered in {DL}'s earlier case over {PRIOR}, {D}'s car was seen parked across from {V}'s workplace on three separate mornings. The security camera records the car each time, parked and waiting.", "The defense will present a man who stops at the coffee shop across the street on his daily route. {D} was buying coffee, not watching {V}, and the shop sits right where {D.his} route takes {D.him}."),
        closings: ("The order told {D} to stay a hundred feet away, and three mornings of a parked car across from the office is not a coincidence. {DL} had already been here over {PRIOR} and knew exactly what the order demanded.", "A coffee shop on {D}'s route explains a parked car better than a plan to watch {V} does. The camera shows a car, never {D} approaching or contacting {V}, and the State has to prove intent beyond a reasonable doubt."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The order is entered."), (0, "Three mornings of the car outside.")],
